{
 "summary": "Checkout failures (gateway 502s, up to 71.8% error ratio) are caused by slow inventory POST /reserve calls. These calls make orders time out with 504s, and the gateway passes those up as 502s. The slowdown began about 15s after inventory was deployed from 3.1.5 to 3.2.1 at 07:18:17Z, and sampled traces put the dominant self time in inventory 3.2.1. Inventory itself returns no 5xx; it is slow, not erroring.",
 "root_cause": {
  "statement": "The inventory 3.2.1 deploy (from 3.1.5) at 07:18:17Z most likely introduced a latency regression in POST /reserve (self time about 2.4-2.6s, p95 up to 4.77s). Orders times out waiting on inventory and returns 504, and the gateway turns those into 502s on POST /checkout. What links the deploy to the symptoms: latency onset at orders/inventory/gateway comes 15-30s after the deploy, and all sampled failing traces run inventory 3.2.1 with the dominant self time there. The specific code or config change is not confirmed because logs are unavailable.",
  "service": "inventory",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "evidence_ids": [
   "ev-190058c637be",
   "ev-5fa58511a1e2",
   "ev-51525d7035d0",
   "ev-1da116a62fee",
   "ev-c000e6b4f684"
  ]
 },
 "contributing_factors": [
  {
   "statement": "Orders appears to enforce a timeout of roughly 2s on its inventory call, returning 504. This turns inventory slowness into hard checkout failures (gateway trace durations 2.01-2.24s).",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-5fa58511a1e2",
    "ev-1da116a62fee"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Orders' error ratio reached 100% by the end of the window, and gateway errors rose to a max of 71.8%.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-1da116a62fee",
    "ev-c000e6b4f684"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "timeline": [
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T07:18:17Z",
   "event": "inventory deployed 3.1.5 -> 3.2.1 by ci-pipeline",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-190058c637be"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T07:18:32.643Z",
   "event": "orders 5xx ratio crosses 5% and p95 latency crosses 1s",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-1da116a62fee"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T07:18:47.643Z",
   "event": "inventory p95 latency crosses 1s; gateway 5xx ratio crosses 5% and p95 crosses 1s",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-51525d7035d0",
    "ev-c000e6b4f684"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T07:20:33Z",
   "event": "Sampled traces show gateway 502 <- orders 504, with dominant self time in inventory POST /reserve (3.2.1); seen through 07:20:43Z",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-5fa58511a1e2"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "ruled_out": [
  {
   "statement": "The gateway is not the origin. It only reports 502s propagated from orders' 504s, and its latency onset follows orders and inventory.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-5fa58511a1e2",
    "ev-c000e6b4f684"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Orders is not the origin. Its 504s are timeouts waiting on inventory, where most trace self time is spent.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-5fa58511a1e2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Inventory is not returning server errors (0% 5xx). The failure mode is latency, not inventory errors.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-51525d7035d0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "A traffic surge is unlikely. Gateway request rate stayed around 2.1-2.5 req/s.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-c000e6b4f684"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "unknowns": [
  "Logs could not be queried (backend timeout), so the internal cause of the inventory slowness is unconfirmed: a code change, a DB or lock contention, or a downstream dependency of inventory.",
  "No traces were sampled before 07:20:33Z, so the self-time attribution covers only the late window.",
  "No inventory dependency metrics (e.g. database) are in the snapshot to rule out a downstream cause coinciding with the deploy.",
  "The orders-to-inventory timeout setting is not directly observed; it is inferred from trace durations."
 ],
 "recommended_actions": [
  {
   "action": "Roll back inventory from 3.2.1 to 3.1.5.",
   "rationale": "The latency onset closely follows this deploy, and the failing traces show the dominant self time in inventory 3.2.1 POST /reserve. A rollback is the fastest test and mitigation.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-190058c637be",
    "ev-5fa58511a1e2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "After the rollback, verify that inventory p95 latency drops below 1s and that orders/gateway 5xx ratios return to baseline.",
   "rationale": "Confirms or refutes the deploy as the cause.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-51525d7035d0",
    "ev-1da116a62fee",
    "ev-c000e6b4f684"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Re-run the log query for inventory and orders over 07:16-07:21Z.",
   "rationale": "Logs were unavailable. They are needed to identify what in 3.2.1 slows POST /reserve and to confirm the orders timeout behavior.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "src-logs"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Inspect example traces e1af7fdd63c588af3940a164158d28c1 and efc519b65a223a76d1b5de89ca1498b3 for child spans under inventory POST /reserve.",
   "rationale": "Shows whether the time is spent in inventory code or in one of its dependencies.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-5fa58511a1e2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Diff the inventory 3.1.5..3.2.1 changes affecting the reserve path.",
   "rationale": "Identifies the specific regression for a fix-forward.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-190058c637be"
   ]
  }
 ]
}
